title: "cellquant: a single-script pipeline for quantitative fluorescence microscopy"
version: "1.1.1"
date-released: "2026-09-02"
license: MIT
type: software
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22239479"
repository-code: "https://github.com/davidpincus/cellquant"
url: "https://github.com/davidpincus/cellquant"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22239479"
    description: "Archived snapshot of cellquant v1.1.1"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21843280"
    description: "Raw fluorescence microscopy z-stacks underlying the published figures"
abstract: >-
  cellquant is a single-script command-line pipeline for quantitative multi-channel
  fluorescence microscopy. It performs cell and nuclear segmentation with Cellpose,
  puncta detection, per-cell intensity and condensation metrics, colocalization, and
  nucleolar proximity and morphology analysis, in either two or three dimensions.
  The interface is entirely text based, so the exact command used to generate any
  result can be recorded and re-executed. It is designed for biologists who do not
  write code and who drive the tool through an AI assistant.
keywords:
  - fluorescence microscopy
  - image analysis
  - cell segmentation
  - Cellpose
  - colocalization
  - biomolecular condensates
  - reproducibility
  - Python
